    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Consistent Array Declarations",
    "description" : "This rule enforces consistent formatting and declaration style for arrays in PHP code, including lowercase 'array' keyword, proper alignment, and trailing commas.",
    "explanation" : "This standard covers all array declarations, regardless of the number and type of values contained within the array.\n\nValid: array keyword lowercase\n```\n$array = array('val1', 'val2');\n```\n\nInvalid: first letter capitalised\n```\n$array = Array('val1', 'val2');\n```\n\nValid: first key on second line\n```\n$array = array(\n          'key1' => 'value1',\n          'key2' => 'value2',\n         );\n```\n\nInvalid: first key on same line\n```\n$array = array('key1' => 'value1',\n          'key2' => 'value2',\n         );\n```\n\nValid: aligned correctly\n```\n$array = array(\n          'key1' => 'value1',\n          'key2' => 'value2',\n         );\n```\n\nInvalid: keys and parenthesis aligned incorrectly\n```\n$array = array(\n         'key1' => 'value1',\n         'key2' => 'value2',\n);\n```\n\nValid: keys and values aligned\n```\n$array = array(\n          'keyTen'    => 'ValueTen',\n          'keyTwenty' => 'ValueTwenty',\n         );\n```\n\nInvalid: alignment incorrect\n```\n$array = array(\n          'keyTen' => 'ValueTen',\n          'keyTwenty' => 'ValueTwenty',\n         );\n```\n\nValid: comma after each value\n```\n$array = array(\n          'key1' => 'value1',\n          'key2' => 'value2',\n          'key3' => 'value3',\n         );\n```\n\nInvalid: no comma after last value\n```\n$array = array(\n          'key1' => 'value1',\n          'key2' => 'value2',\n          'key3' => 'value3' \n         );\n```",
